    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Lake Superior, the largest freshwater lake in the world, has an area of $82\\,732\\text{ km}^2$. The second largest, Lake Victoria, has an area of $69\\,753\\text{ km}^2$. How much larger is Lake Superior?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$12\\,979\\text{ km}^2$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{array}{r}82\\,732\\\\-\\,69\\,753\\\\\\hline12\\,979\\\\\\hline\\end{array}$$\n\nCheck: $69\\,753+12\\,979=82\\,732$.\n\nLake Superior is $12\\,979\\text{ km}^2$ larger.",
